.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH quarters-enter 1  "quarters-enter " 
.SH NAME
quarters\-enter \- Enter an interactive shell in a space
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBquarters\-enter\fR [\fB\-\-home\-view\fR] [\fB\-\-confinement\fR] [\fB\-\-inherit\fR] [\fB\-\-grant\-path\fR] [\fB\-\-workdir\fR] [\fB\-\-shell\fR] [\fB\-\-login\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fINAME\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Enter an interactive shell in a space
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-home\-view\fR
Opt into Linux\*(Aqs experimental bind\-mounted passwd\-home view
.TP
\fB\-\-confinement\fR \fI<CONFINEMENT>\fR
Enforce the named native filesystem policy; defaults to the Quarter home
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
filesystem: Linux Landlock ABI 3 path policy; unavailable on macOS
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-inherit\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Explicitly inherit one otherwise\-blocked host environment variable
.TP
\fB\-\-grant\-path\fR \fI<ABSOLUTE_PATH:ro|rw>\fR
Admit one existing absolute host data path to Linux confinement
.TP
\fB\-\-workdir\fR \fI<ABSOLUTE_PATH>\fR
Start the shell or command in this existing absolute directory
.TP
\fB\-\-shell\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Override the space\*(Aqs default shell for this entry
.TP
\fB\-\-login\fR
Ask the shell for login behavior. This may run host system profiles
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fINAME\fR>
Space to inspect or launch
